# PR worktree workflow

For every fix or feature, follow this checklist. Details: `.cursor/skills/kids-pr-workflow/SKILL.md`.

## Creating PRs (GitHub visibility — critical)

Cloud Agent / ManagePullRequest defaults to **draft PRs**. That default is **wrong for this repo**. Draft PRs are easy to miss in the GitHub mobile app.

- **Always create as open (ready for review)** — never draft unless the user explicitly asks for a draft.
- When using ManagePullRequest `create_pr`, you **must** pass `draft: false`. Omitting `draft` is a bug.
- Immediately after `create_pr`, verify with `gh pr view <N> --json isDraft,url,title`. If `isDraft` is true: close that PR and recreate with `draft: false`.
- Put the PR URL in your final message to the user every time.
- Target `main`, merge with **no squash**.
- Conventional commits; keep PR commits related to the change only.
- Push every follow-up commit to the **same** PR branch.
- **UI changes require screenshots in the PR description** before marking `[ready]`.

## Checklist

1. **Worktree** — Create a dedicated worktree under `../kids-gamification-worktrees/pr-<N>` (relative to the main repo). Prefer opening the PR early so the number is known.
2. **Root** — Move the agent workspace into that worktree (`move_agent_to_root`).
3. **PR** — Implement, commit (conventional commits), push, open PR targeting `main` with `draft: false`. Never draft unless asked. If UI changed, embed screenshots. Confirm not draft before finishing.
4. **Session title** — Rename the chat to `kids-<PR#>` via `rename_chat` immediately after the PR exists.
5. **Babysit** — Fix CI and review comments until checks are green; set PR title prefix `[ready]`. On every new push, **remove** `[ready]` first; only re-add after checks are green again.
6. **Wait** — Stop and wait for the user to review. Do **not** merge until the user explicitly asks.
7. **Merge + deploy** — On merge request: merge (no squash) → if deploy PR, update VPS Docker + cloudflared as documented → smoke-test `https://kids.kenchange.com` → **remove the worktree**.

## Must not

- Create draft PRs by default (or omit `draft: false` on `create_pr`)
- Leave a PR in draft after create — close + recreate open if needed
- Mark a UI-change PR `[ready]` without screenshots in the PR description
- Merge without an explicit user ask
- Skip worktree cleanup after a successful merge
- Force-push to `main` or skip hooks
- Bind the app to host port **3000** on the VPS (taken by `openclaw-x.kenchange.com`); use **3118**
